"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[87834],{87834:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<RestaurantCard\\n  cover=\\"/assets/snippets/location/7eb23f0631873ded35bf2fb3e99f182d.jpg\\"\\n  title=\\"Suwol Gyeonghwa\\"\\n  cuisine=\\"Cafe\\"\\n  address=\\"188 Songjeongjungang-ro 6beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan\\"\\n  rating=3\\n  tags=\\"cafe\\"\\n/>\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nI visited this place after traveling on the `Haeundae Beach Train`.  \\nIt wasn\'t a place I visited with high expectations, but the view was much better than I thought.  \\n\\nAt the entrance, there was a decoration showing the cafe\'s identity.  \\nCompared to the atmosphere at the entrance, the interior felt surprisingly clean and modern.  \\n\\nSeeing a note that they serve it with an egg yolk, I ordered `ssanghwa-tang` (traditional herbal tea) and an `iced americano` without hesitation.  \\n\\nThe `ssanghwa-tang` was on the sweeter side and was packed with nuts.  \\nPersonally, I thought it could have been a bit less sweet.  \\n\\nOn the contrary, the coffee suited my taste better as it was savory with low acidity.  \\n\\nI spent a relaxing time sitting in a spot perfect for spacing out while looking at the sea.\\n## Pictures\\n<pictures>\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/4cc1030126f60fcecfd53aa64b1bd0ff.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Suwol Gyeonghwa\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/cd4476741ab45af6c414a9ec071bcb71.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Suwol Gyeonghwa\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/5da6a787c11868413da273a0d24b4407.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Suwol Gyeonghwa\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/f0f2c092266183aaf6989cdb6cede80f.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Suwol Gyeonghwa\\">\\n</pictures>\\n"}')}}]);